-- EXPECT-ERROR: Only public functions of
-- Slice 6 (proof caps), the mint_cap UNFORGEABILITY witness (external module)
-- -- `mint_cap` is the ONLY sanctioned way to construct a proof cap, and it is
-- gated to a PUBLIC fn of the cap's DECLARING module. Here `App` (a non-
-- declaring module) tries to `mint_cap` a `Cap(Db.P)`; because the mint sits
-- in the fn's declared RETURN position, Check 6 (the declared-return-type
-- pass-through discipline) fires FIRST -- `App` did not receive `Cap(Db.P)`
-- as a parameter and is not `Db`, so it may only pass the cap through, never
-- construct it. Together the mint gate + Check 6 mean a foreign module can
-- never mint a proof cap. IMPOSSIBLE to reject pre-fix (pre-slice `mint_cap`
-- did not exist; the equivalent `cap_narrow` forge accepted). See
-- core-march-types.md §2.8.13. Accept companion: `accept/t62` (the same mint
-- INSIDE `Db`'s public fn accepts).
mod Sys do
  mod Db do
    proof cap P
  end

  mod App do
    needs IO
    needs Db.P

    fn make(cap : Cap(IO)) : Cap(Db.P) do mint_cap(cap) end
  end
end
